    "bottomLine": "The best way to get a brushless, genuinely capable drill without paying pro-platform prices.",
    "description": "The PBLDD01 is Ryobi's ONE+ HP brushless 1/2-inch drill/driver, and it is the value pick because it delivers most of what a homeowner will ever ask of a drill for noticeably less money than the pro brands. Ryobi rates it at up to 750 in-lbs of torque and a two-speed range of 0-500 and 0-2,100 RPM, with a 24-position clutch that gives you more fine steps than most drills on this page. As always, Ryobi's torque figure is its own rating, so do not read it as proof that it out-twists drills from brands that publish lower or no numbers. The kit version, PBLDD01K1, comes with a 2.0Ah battery and charger; that battery keeps the drill light but runs down quickly on big spade bits or a long afternoon of deck screws, so a 4.0Ah pack is a worthwhile add. The bigger argument for this drill is the platform. ONE+ batteries fit a very large family of tools, from inflators to string trimmers, which makes Ryobi the cheapest way to fill a garage. Our Ryobi tools review covers where the line is genuinely good and where it is not. For weekend projects and home repair, this drill is plenty."
  },
