        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy the platform first and the drill second. For most people that means a compact brushless DeWalt DCD800 or, if you want the most headroom, the Milwaukee M18 FUEL 2903-20. Ryobi's PBLDD01 is the value choice, the M12 FUEL 3403-20 is the drill for tight spaces, and the Makita XPH14 is the one to get if you drill masonry.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Ignore cross-brand torque comparisons, read the model suffix so you know whether batteries are included, and plan for a matching impact driver. Get those three things right and any drill on this list will serve you for years.
          </p>
